<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6371" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cambȳses</span></b> , is,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Καμβύσης</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>The husband of Mandane</i>, <i>and
				father of the elder Cyrus</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 1, 4,
				4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The son and successor of the elder Cyrus</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 1,
			9</span></i>; Mel.  1, 11, 3; <i><span class="en">Val. Max. 6,
			3</span></i>, ext. 3; <i><span class="en">Luc. 10, 280</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A river in Albania</i>, <i>which rises
				on the Caucasus and empties into the Cyrus</i>, now <i>Jora</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 3, 5, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 13,
				15, § 39</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A river of Media</i>, <i><span class="en">Amm.
				23, 6, 40</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
